{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 11,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.138,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "110"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.152,
            0.898,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the coordinates of the points of trisection of the line segment joining A and B are (−1, 0) and (− 4, 2)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.2,
            0.899,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": "Note : We could also have obtained Q by noting that it is the mid-point of PB. So, we could have obtained its coordinates using the mid-point formula."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.255,
            0.899,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "Example 9 : Find the ratio in which the y-axis divides the line segment joining the points (5, – 6) and (–1, – 4). Also find the point of intersection."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.304,
            0.898,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": "Solution : Let the ratio be k : 1. Then by the section formula, the coordinates of the point which divides AB in the ratio k : 1 are $\\left( \\frac{-k + 5}{k + 1}, \\frac{-4k - 6}{k + 1} \\right)$ ed"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.392,
            0.835,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "This point lies on the y-axis, and we know that on the y-axis the abscissa is 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.437,
            0.205,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.386,
            0.425,
            0.508,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "\\frac { - k + 5 } { k + 1 } = 0",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.481,
            0.135,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.479,
            0.508,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "k \\equiv 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.505,
            0.898,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "That is, the ratio is 5 : 1. Putting the value of $k = 5 ,$ we get the point of intersection as $\\left(0, \\frac{-13}{3}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.595,
            0.9,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "Example 10 : If the points A(6, 1), B(8, 2), C(9, 4) and $\\mathrm { D } ( p , 3 )$ are the vertices of a parallelogram, taken in order, find the value of $\\left[ p \\right]$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.645,
            0.788,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "Solution : We know that diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.673,
            0.862,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "So, the coordinates of the mid-point of AC = coordinates of the mid-point of BD"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.721,
            0.139,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.706,
            0.645,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{6 + 9}{2}, \\frac{1 + 4}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{8 + p}{2}, \\frac{2 + 3}{2} \\right)",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.786,
            0.138,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.377,
            0.769,
            0.608,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{15}{2}, \\frac{5}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{8 + p}{2}, \\frac{5}{2} \\right)",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.848,
            0.131,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "SO,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.429,
            0.831,
            0.555,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": "\\left[ { \\frac { 1 5 } { 2 } } = { \\frac { 8 + p } { 2 } } \\right]",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.883,
            0.138,
            0.9
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.882,
            0.508,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": "p = 7",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
